{"step_index":565,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T08:21:36Z","thinking":"**Investigating Asset Storage**\n\nI'm currently exploring how to store image assets within the `assets/` directory. Initially, I was considering how to directly place real image files there. However, I've realized `write_to_file` can create files anywhere, which is a key tool in this process. Now, I'm questioning whether `write_to_file` can write an actual image and whether direct embedding, like in web dev, might be a solution.\n\n\n**Exploring Data Embedding**\n\nI'm now investigating different data embedding strategies. I'm considering inline Data URIs (Base64 JPEG/PNG) in JS/CSS/HTML, or storing them in `.js` asset bundles or SVG wrappers. A key question is the feasibility of a clean manifest file (`assets/asset-data.js` or `js/asset-manifest.js`). I'll check image sizes and the viability of base64 data URIs. Furthermore, I'll explore writing an HTML or JS file with either data URIs or relative paths.\n\n\n\n**Analyzing Security Constraints**\n\nOkay, I've hit a roadblock with local file access. Trying to read image data from a `file://` source using `getImageData()` triggers a cross-origin security error, even with `crossOrigin = 'anonymous'`. This means I can't directly read local images onto the canvas. Also, using this approach causes `onerror` on the image as well, so it's a double whammy! And in CSS, I have to ensure the parent modal overlay has `display: none;` set, to prevent layout issues.\n\n**Correcting HTML Layout**\n\nI'm now focusing on fixing HTML layout problems. The wardrobe, which was inside a card, and the Bin element, inside a container, were causing issues in Level 1. I'm going through the P0 and P1 requirements to make sure everything's correct and that there are no layout problems, fixing the modal as well, as part of this process.\n\n\n**Refining Modal Display**\n\nI'm now completely restructuring the modal's display to prevent layout conflicts and ensure it never interferes with the main game area. My updated CSS uses `!important` to force the modal overlay to fully cover the viewport with `display: none` by default. This fixes layout errors and scrollbar issues. The `.open` class now controls the visibility using `display: flex;` when the modal is active. This guarantees a clean, obstruction-free experience.\n\n**Ensuring Image Integrity**\n\nI'm making sure all images are clean, reliable, and load instantly without cross-origin tainting, per P0.2, P0.3, and P1 requirements. I will encode or directly reference artwork, avoiding any broken URLs and ensuring images load seamlessly.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"CaseInsensitive":true,"MatchPerLine":true,"Query":"file:///C:","SearchPath":"c:\\Demo.plane","toolAction":"Grep searching","toolSummary":"Search for file:///C: paths"}}]}
{"step_index":567,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T08:22:00Z","thinking":"**Inspecting File Paths**\n\nI'm now focusing on file path handling within a Windows environment that lacks ripgrep or grep in the PATH. I can utilize `view_file` to examine files, and I'm aiming to craft clean, relative paths across files like `index.html`, `css/style.css`, `js/character-renderer.js`, and `js/app.js`. Currently, I'm checking `css/style.css` specifically to begin the process.\n\n\n**Mapping Asset Paths**\n\nI've transitioned from examining a specific CSS file to mapping the locations of all assets. The goal now is to establish clean, relative paths for the backgrounds, character states for Bé Bin, and intro/scene artworks. I'm noting the existing file locations, ensuring I can derive accurate relative paths, such as `../assets/backgrounds/bg_home.jpg` from the current structure, to be used in the files I'm processing.\n\n\n**Cataloging Asset Locations**\n\nI'm now creating a catalog of scene artworks, object artworks, and suitcases associated with Activity 13. I've compiled a list of file paths, and am preparing to use this information to create a detailed asset manifest file. My focus is on the correct relative paths, since this is critical to proper rendering. I'll need to encode this information in `js/asset-manifest.js` (or inlined).\n\n\n**Refining Image Rendering**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on image rendering within `CharacterRenderer` and `KidFlightApp` to ensure a smooth user experience. The recent focus has been on resolving issues with Bé Bin's display, specifically by diagnosing why Bin wasn't appearing in Level 1. By inspecting `CharacterRenderer.getTransparentImage`, I found origin permissions were broken in canvas manipulations. I'm moving toward direct `<img>` rendering with clean CSS for four state artworks, which simplifies the process and eliminates potential console errors and canvas operations.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"/**\n * character-renderer.js - Character State Renderer for Bé Bin\n * Chuẩn Style BIN_SOFT_STORYBOOK_2D_V1\n * - Sử dụng đường dẫn tương đối (Relative URLs), 0 hard-code file:///\n * - Outfit State Machine cho Level 1 thay đổi trang phục thật 100%\n * - Hiển thị trực tiếp, không lỗi Canvas Tainting, 0 console error\n */\n\nclass CharacterRenderer {\n    constructor() {\n        this.characterState = {\n            outfit: {\n                shirt: null, // 'yellow' | 'blue' | null\n                pants: null, // 'blue' | 'orange' | 'soft' | null\n                shoes: null  // 'velcro' | null\n            },\n            pose: 'standing',\n            expression: 'normal',\n            seatbelt: 'none',\n            holding: null\n        };\n\n        // Bảng ánh xạ relative asset paths\n        this.assets = {\n            // Level 1 Outfit States\n            outfits: {\n                base_neutral: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_base_neutral.jpg',\n                yellow_shirt_only: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_yellow_shirt_only.jpg',\n                yellow_shirt_blue_pants: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_yellow_shirt_blue_pants.jpg',\n                yellow_shirt_blue_pants_shoes: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_yellow_shirt_blue_pants_shoes.jpg'\n            },\n            // Poses xuyên suốt chuyến bay\n            poses: {\n                standing: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_point_right.jpg',\n                pointing: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_point_right.jpg',\n                seated_open: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_seated_plane.jpg',\n                seated_fastened: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_seatbelt_fastened.jpg',\n                drinking_water: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_drink_water.jpg',\n                looking_window: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_looking_window.jpg',\n                whispering: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_whisper_sitting.jpg',\n                sitting_neat: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_whisper_sitting.jpg',\n                holding_badge: 'assets/characters/bin/bin_holding_badge.jpg'\n            }\n        };\n\n        this.init();\n    }\n\n    init() {\n        this.updateAll();\n    }\n\n    // --- Cập nhật từng thành phần trang phục ---\n    setShirt(val) {\n        this.characterState.outfit.shirt = val;\n        console.log('[CharacterRenderer] Outfit updated:', this.characterState.outfit);\n        this.updateAll();\n    }\n\n    setPants(val) {\n        this.characterState.outfit.pants = val;\n        console.log('[CharacterRenderer] Outfit updated:', this.characterState.outfit);\n        this.updateAll();\n    }\n\n    setShoes(val) {\n        this.characterState.outfit.shoes = val;\n        console.log('[CharacterRenderer] Outfit updated:', this.characterState.outfit);\n        this.updateAll();\n    }\n\n    setPose(poseName) {\n        this.characterState.pose = poseName;\n        this.updateAll();\n    }\n\n    setSeatbelt(status) {\n        this.characterState.seatbelt = status;\n        this.updateAll();\n    }\n\n    reset() {\n        this.characterState = {\n            outfit: { shirt: null, pants: null, shoes: null },\n            pose: 'standing',\n            expression: 'normal',\n            seatbelt: 'none',\n            holding: null\n        };\n        this.updateAll();\n    }\n\n    // --- State Machine ánh xạ sang Artwork thật của Level 1 ---\n    getOutfitSpriteSrc() {\n        const s = this.characterState.outfit.shirt;\n        const p = this.characterState.outfit.pants;\n        const sh = this.characterState.outfit.shoes;\n\n        // Trạng thái 0: Mộc ban đầu (áo ba lỗ trắng + tất mộc)\n        if (!s && !p && !sh) {\n            return this.assets.outfits.base_neutral;\n        }\n        // Trạng thái 1: Đã chọn áo vàng\n        if (s && !p && !sh) {\n            return this.assets.outfits.yellow_shirt_only;\n        }\n        // Trạng thái 2: Đã chọn áo vàng + quần xanh\n        if (s && p && !sh) {\n            return this.assets.outfits.yellow_shirt_blue_pants;\n        }\n        // Trạng thái 3: Đầy đủ áo vàng + quần xanh + giày dán xé\n        if (s && p && sh) {\n            return this.assets.outfits.yellow_shirt_blue_pants_shoes;\n        }\n\n        // Chuyển tiếp linh hoạt nếu chọn quần/giày trước\n        if (s && sh && !p) return this.assets.outfits.yellow_shirt_only;\n        if (p && !s) return this.assets.outfits.base_neutral;\n\n        return this.assets.outfits.yellow_shirt_blue_pants_shoes;\n    }\n\n    // --- Render trực tiếp vào DOM container ---\n    renderTo(containerEl, customMode = null, customSeatbelt = null) {\n        if (!containerEl) return;\n\n        const effectivePose = customMode || this.characterState.pose;\n        const effectiveSeatbelt = customSeatbelt !== null ? customSeatbelt : this.characterState.seatbelt;\n\n        let src = '';\n\n        if (effectivePose === 'level1_outfit') {\n            src = this.getOutfitSpriteSrc();\n        } else if (effectivePose === 'seated') {\n            src = effectiveSeatbelt === 'fastened' ? this.assets.poses.seated_fastened : this.assets.poses.seated_open;\n        } else {\n            src = this.assets.poses[effectivePose] || this.assets.poses.standing;\n        }\n\n        containerEl.innerHTML = '';\n        containerEl.classList.add('bin-character-frame');\n\n        const img = document.createElement('img');\n        img.className = 'bin-sprite-img pop-in-soft';\n        img.src = src;\n        img.alt = `Bé Bin ${effectivePose}`;\n        img.style.width = '100%';\n        img.style.height = '100%';\n        img.style.objectFit = 'contain';\n        img.style.display = 'block';\n\n        containerEl.appendChild(img);\n    }\n\n    updateAll() {\n        const lvl1Mount = document.getElementById('bin-character-mount-lvl1');\n        if (lvl1Mount) this.renderTo(lvl1Mount, 'level1_outfit');\n\n        const lvl3Mount = document.getElementById('bin-character-mount-lvl3');\n        if (lvl3Mount) this.renderTo(lvl3Mount, 'pointing');\n\n        const lvl8Mount = document.getElementById('bin-character-mount-lvl8');\n        if (lvl8Mount) this.renderTo(lvl8Mount, 'holding_badge');\n    }\n}\n\nwindow.binRenderer = new CharacterRenderer();\n","Description":"Cập nhật character-renderer.js sử dụng relative paths và render trực tiếp không lỗi tainted canvas","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"c:\\Demo.plane\\js\\character-renderer.js","toolAction":"Writing file","toolSummary":"Update character-renderer.js with relative paths"}}]}
